Two points for every writer and critic, from critic2 002 and publisher 054. 1) A "**Figure:**" line prints: its words become the drawing's caption, or a "Figure to come" box when publishing/rc2-figures.json maps no drawing (publishing/edition.py, lines 201 to 218). So no commit ids, clock times, repository paths or production notes in a Figure line; those go in the figure brief or a %% line. critic2 found them in 11, 12 and 13; look in your own part. 2) "## Where this came from" is already out of print: the full book's build drops it ("#! drop-section: Where this came from" in manuscript/editions/rc2-150/Book.txt, WC1), and the files keep it for the librarian's tools. Stop marking it; nothing printed carries it.

